# netaddr.rc — the D-11 single addressing seam for the Phase-8 net gates.
#
# One committed harness-side data file defines guest/host addresses per
# leg; every later gate's assertions and baked fragments derive from it —
# sourced by the root-tree/lib/netip-*.rc sweeps (08-04/06/07/08) and read
# by the r9 xtask profiles through the R9_HARVEY_DIR channel.  NO gate
# hardcodes a 10.0.2.x or other per-leg address anywhere else (Pitfall 9's
# named failure mode).  Phase 9 lifts this seam into HNET-02's TOML
# single-sourcing.
#
# Shape: rc-syntax key=value assignments, one commented section per leg,
# keys prefixed by leg so sourcing the whole file binds every leg
# unambiguously (a bare guestv4 per leg would be last-wins on source).
# Consumers take the leg prefix they serve.

# --- loopback leg (08-04/05 gates: ping 127.0.0.1, udp echo, tcp/7 echo,
#     aan drop-and-resume — all NIC-free) ---
lo_guestv4=127.0.0.1

# --- slirp leg (08-06/07/08 gates: static ipconfig, DHCP via ipconfig's
#     dhcpclient, ether-leg IPv6, the tcpblast machinery proof) ---
# qemu -netdev user defaults: vnetwork 10.0.2.0/24, host 10.0.2.2, guest
# 10.0.2.15 (DHCP start).  Hermetic/unprivileged/CI-able; every slirp-green
# gate is labeled not-L2-truth per D-10 — the tap verdict is Phase 9's
# joint gate (D-15).
slirp_guestv4=10.0.2.15
slirp_maskv4=255.255.255.0
slirp_gwv4=10.0.2.2
# slirp v6: qemu's default v6 prefix is fec0::/64 with the host at fec0::2
# and the guest at fec0::15.  FINALIZED from the 08-07 probe run
# (2026-11-06, R9_NETIP_SWEEP=v6 on the live gate): slirp answers ND for
# fec0::2 (the guest's NS got an NA) AND serves ICMPv6 echo there (3/3
# echo replies); it emitted NO unsolicited RAs in the gate window (the
# only non-echo/ND v6 frame was the guest's own MLDv2 solicited-node
# group-join report at the address add).  host→guest v6 reachability is
# deferred to Phase 9's tap leg per D-10/D-15 (no hostfwd this phase).
slirp_guestv6=fec0::15
slirp_gwv6=fec0::2

# tcpblast host-echo port (the 08-08 slirp soak dials slirp_gwv4:blastport;
# the sweep owns the host-side echo listener on this port).
blastport=7777
